# Grant the logged-in user access to the N-SL SW001 IMU evdev node.
# The gamepad joystick node gets a uaccess ACL via Steam's rules, but the
# separate "Pro Controller (IMU)" input node does not, leaving SDL unable to
# open it (EACCES), so SDL_GamepadHasSensor(ACCEL/GYRO) is always false.
#
# TAG+="seat" is needed too: 71-seat.rules propagates uaccess->seat for
# tag==uaccess devices, but it runs at priority 71, BEFORE this 99 rule, so
# the seat tag never arrives and the uaccess ACL is not applied.
#
# The ACL from uaccess/seat alone is racy on reconnect: logind stamps
# SYSTEMD_SEAT and applies the ACL asynchronously, after udev has already
# created the node and SDL has tried to open it.  The RUN setfacl applies
# the ACL synchronously inside the ADD event, before SDL gets a chance.
# The user is resolved from the seat's active session (no hardcoded name).
SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ATTRS{name}=="Pro Controller (IMU)", \
  TAG+="uaccess", TAG+="seat", \
  RUN+="/bin/sh -c 'u=$$(loginctl show-seat seat0 -p ActiveSession --value 2>/dev/null); u=$$(loginctl show-session $$u -p Name --value 2>/dev/null); setfacl -m u:$$u:rw /dev/input/%k'"
